Parameter:
  (<Article number>)

Description:
  Adds a footnote to an article that you wrote. The footnote is shown
  as a separate addition when the article is read.

  If no article number is given, the article you last read in the
  current conference is used. If you give an article number, the
  footnote is added to that article.

  The footnote is written in the text editor and may contain several
  lines. Save it with Ctrl-Z.

Please note:
  You can only add footnotes to your own articles.

  Footnotes are only available in local conferences, not in your
  Mailbox, Usenet conferences, or FTN conferences.

  An article can only have one footnote. If a footnote already exists,
  the command stops without changing the existing footnote.

  When no article number is given, the last article you read must
  belong to the conference you are currently visiting.

Background:
  The footnote feature was added in October 2025. Internally, each
  line is appended to the article file with the prefix F:. When the
  article is displayed, these lines are collected in a separate
  footnote block.
